Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: qcom: msm_gpi: reject timed-out event commands before channel fallback

gpi_alloc_ev_chan() calls gpi_send_cmd() with a NULL channel argument.
Event commands use the GPII event registers and do not have a channel.
The command timeout fallback nevertheless calls gpi_read_ch_state()
unconditionally, dereferencing that NULL argument.

Report an event command timeout and return -EIO before the channel-only
fallback. Keep the existing channel fallback and successful command paths
unchanged. This prevents the secondary NULL dereference; it does not make
the timed-out command succeed or repair the underlying completion failure.

Applies to the OnePlus vendor driver drivers/dma/qcom/msm_gpi.c, including
reference revision 4553152f62a3bd9f39bb6d068a4d94a15a8c07fd. The generic
common-kernel drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c is a different driver. Rebuilding and
deploying a matching msm_gpi.ko is required for this change to take effect.

diff --git a/drivers/dma/qcom/msm_gpi.c b/drivers/dma/qcom/msm_gpi.c
--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/msm_gpi.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/msm_gpi.c
@@ -1700,6 +1700,12 @@ static int gpi_send_cmd(struct gpii *gpii,
 	if (!timeout) {
 		offset = GPI_GPII_n_CNTXT_TYPE_IRQ_OFFS(gpii->gpii_id);
 		irq_stat = gpi_read_reg(gpii, gpii->regs + offset);
+		if (!IS_CHAN_CMD(gpi_cmd)) {
+			GPII_ERR(gpii, chid,
+				 "event cmd: %s completion timeout irq_status=0x%x\n",
+				 TO_GPI_CMD_STR(gpi_cmd), irq_stat);
+			return -EIO;
+		}
 		state = gpi_read_ch_state(gpii_chan);
 		/* Fallback mechanism for verifying the state of the register */
 		if (irq_stat & GPI_GPII_n_CNTXT_TYPE_IRQ_MSK_CH_CTRL) {
